CloudBurrow patch 20 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1401). Applies after patch 0019; needs
googlesqlite patch 0031.

The gap: a value written to a parameterized NUMERIC(P, S) or
BIGNUMERIC(P, S) column is kept at its full scale, and one with more than
P digits is kept. BigQuery rounds it to S digits by the column's
roundingMode, else the table's defaultRoundingMode, else
ROUND_HALF_AWAY_FROM_ZERO, and raises OUT_OF_RANGE past the precision
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/data-types#parameterized_decimal_type,
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/schemas#rounding_mode).

The patch makes, each time a table's resource is written (tables.insert,
update, patch, a query's DDL) and when its engine table is made, SQLite
triggers AFTER INSERT and AFTER UPDATE OF each such top-level column that
call googlesqlite_round_decimal, so every write path (DML, insertAll,
loads, the Storage Write API, query destinations) rounds.

